OL,3,GNEWSALeader denies parking charge hike
OL,4,Ais 'cash cow'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe leader of Liverpool Council has
OL,7,Fdefended the second increase in car
OL,8,Fparking charges in 12 months, insisting
OL,9,Ffees and fines are not being used as a
OL,10,F"cash cow."
OL,12,FThe cost of parking on street in the
OL,13,Fcity centre for half an hour has gone
OL,14,Fup by 10p to #2.40 while a two-hour
OL,15,Fstay is now #6.80.
OL,17,FSome businesses have claimed the
OL,18,Fincrease in charges has affected trade.
OL,19,FChef Paul Askew, who runs a city centre
OL,20,Frestaurant, described it as "another
OL,21,Fdeath knell for hospitality".
OL,23,APub: 04-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,406,400,260,160,0,100
